<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Tell</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wilhelm Tell</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Tell is the legendary hero of the founding of the Swiss Confederacy, a marksman from Uri said to have been forced by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> bailiff Gessler to shoot an apple from his son's head at Altdorf. He then killed Gessler. The story is first recorded around 1470 in the White Book of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarnen">Sarnen</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedrich-schiller">Friedrich Schiller</a>'s play of 1804 and Rossini's opera of 1829 made it famous.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-tell.jpg" alt="William Tell" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Sandreuter; photograph: Roland zh · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Landesmuseum_Z%C3%BCrich_2010-09-20_14-38-14_ShiftN.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
